  "issue_number": 5255,
  "issue_title": "fix: IndexNow's 48h window guarantees duplicate submission of every changed URL",
  "issue_body": "## Goal\nFix `indexnow-scheduled.ts`'s change-detection window so it stops guaranteeing duplicate submission of essentially every changed URL, which directly contradicts the job's own anti-spam design comment.\n\n## Why this matters\nThe job's own header comment states: *\"We submit ONLY the URLs that changed recently... resubmitting unchanged URLs gives no benefit and reads as spam.\"* But the job runs daily (`DAILY_CRON = \"0 5 * * *\"`, 24h cadence) using a 48-hour change-detection window (`WINDOW_MS = 48 * 60 * 60 * 1000`) \u2014 exactly 2x the cadence. Traced the arithmetic: an entry updated shortly after one run has `age < 48h` at both the next run (24h later) and the run after that (48h later), so it's submitted twice before correctly aging out on the third run. This isn't an edge case \u2014 it's the guaranteed common case for essentially every changed URL, directly contradicting the \"resubmitting reads as spam\" rationale the comment itself states.\n\n## Current behavior\n`apps/web/plugins/indexnow-scheduled.ts:10,18,63-91` uses a 48h sliding window against a 24h run cadence, guaranteeing double submission of every changed URL under normal operation.\n\n## Desired behavior\nEither:\n(a) shrink the window close to the actual cadence (e.g. 25-26h \u2014 just enough tolerance for one occasionally-missed daily run, without doubling submissions in the normal case), or\n(b) track a persisted \"last submitted\" watermark (e.g. in KV or D1) instead of a pure sliding time window, so a URL is submitted exactly once per real change regardless of run timing.\n\nOption (a) is the narrower fix; option (b) is more robust against missed/delayed runs but requires new persisted state \u2014 pick based on how much missed-run tolerance actually matters in practice.\n\n## Scope\n- apps/web/plugins/indexnow-scheduled.ts\n- focused tests: tests/indexnow.test.ts, tests/indexnow-submit-args.test.ts\n\n## Out of scope\n- indexnow-hubs.test.ts / indexnow-normalize-site-url.test.ts's covered logic (unrelated to the window calculation)\n- Any change to which URLs are eligible for submission beyond the window/watermark logic itself\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- PR includes `Closes #<issue>`.\n- A URL updated once is submitted exactly once across the normal daily run cadence (barring the explicitly-tolerated missed-run case, if choosing option (a)).\n- The chosen fix's reasoning (window size chosen, or watermark design) is documented in a code comment, matching the file's existing comment style.\n- A regression test proves a URL updated at T+\u03b5 is not submitted on both the T+24h and T+48h runs under the new logic.\n\n## Quality evidence required in the PR\n- No visual impact.\n- Include a before/after: trace of a URL's submission eligibility across 3 consecutive daily runs, showing double-submission before and single-submission after.\n\n## Validation\npnpm exec vitest run tests/indexnow.test.ts tests/indexnow-submit-args.test.ts\n",
